regress\artifacts\armbfiwidth\codex_fixdesign_20260910.txt:1:VERDICT: use a three-way mask: zero for invalid ordering, then #510’s full-width/unsigned-shift expression. Require full-width, both width-31, negative-width, zero-width, interior, and one-bit boundary rows. The 468/465 counts are correct; another unsafe mask site remains outside ARM.
regress\artifacts\armbfiwidth\codex_fixdesign_20260910.txt:41:The history search returned `c0c7f55`, `01a0339`, and `eb83992`. At both repaired mask sites, #510’s operative line is **verbatim**:
regress\artifacts\armbfiwidth\codex_fixdesign_20260910.txt:54:See the [#510 changelog block](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/CHANGELOG.md:1248).
regress\artifacts\armbfiwidth\codex_fixdesign_20260910.txt:101:- Invalid-order rows with zero source and zero destination can likewise pass despite the defect. The contrasting seeds above avoid that particular weakness under the count-masked lowering discussed by #510.
regress\artifacts\armbfiwidth\codex_fixdesign_20260910.txt:110:The project-root [sanitizer Makefile](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/build-asan/Makefile:9) contains `-fsanitize=address,undefined`. However, the current probe does not assert absence of sanitizer diagnostics in its captured transcript. **Using that binary alone does not turn its register-value assertions into a definedness check.** That requires a diagnostic oracle or an explicit static check.
regress\artifacts\armbfiwidth\codex_fixdesign_20260910.txt:117:| [m88k `m88k_rot`](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_m88k_instr.c:513) | Exact sibling: `(1 << n) - 1`. The nonzero guard permits `n == 31`; signed-shift UB remains. #510 already explicitly recorded this. |
regress\artifacts\armbfiwidth\codex_fixdesign_20260910.txt:118:| [MIPS `ext` and `dext`](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_mips_instr.c:1752) | Computed complementary shift counts remain unsafe. Enumeration finds 496 negative counts for EXT, and 496 each for DEXTM/DEXTU. Casting a negative count to `uint64_t` does not make it valid. |
regress\artifacts\armbfiwidth\codex_fixdesign_20260910.txt:122:ARM also retains the separate signed bitmap shifts at lines 2775 and 2913. Consequently, **“third of three” describes the ARM mask subset, not a tree-wide absence of remaining shift defects**. The history also shows BFI was explicitly deferred by #510, rather than unnoticed.
