regress\artifacts\armbfxwidth32\panel_p1_20260907\ollama_glm.txt:1103:8. **What the guest observes (section 2 item 3): the guess is correctly labeled.** Under the named lowering (count mod 32): UBFX #0,#32 → rd = 0 (should be rn); SBFX #0,#32 → rd = 0. Under other lowerings (e.g., count saturating to 0-shift result 0 → mask 0xffffffff), the code is accidentally CORRECT at width 32. So the miscompare is host-dependent — which is the point of UB. Also width==31: on gcc/clang-style fold (wrap to 0x80000000), mask = 0x7fffffff → correct; so no observable wrongness at 31 on those hosts, only UB (and UBSan traps). The named measurement not inlined: UBSan build (`-fsanitize=shift-base`) executing `UBFX rd,rn,#0,#31` then `#0,#32` — expected trap on both — or reading rd after `#0,#32` on the project's host.
