regress\artifacts\armbfxwidth32\codex_fixcheck_20260907.txt:41:| **No-op / preserve destination** — 1 decision | [cpu_mips_instr.c, `X(ins)`](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_mips_instr.c:1730) is the closest bitfield analogue. Its shift count `32 - pos - size` simplifies to `31 - msb`, always 0–31. When `msb < pos`, the mask becomes zero. It preserves the destination’s low 32 bits; the final `int32_t` conversion means this is not necessarily a whole-register no-op in the 64-bit variant. This behavior follows from the code, rather than an explicit policy comment. |
regress\artifacts\armbfxwidth32\codex_fixcheck_20260907.txt:55:- **Additional source findings:** [M88K `m88k_rot`](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_m88k_instr.c:508) retains the signed-mask expression, and [MIPS `X(ext)`](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_mips_instr.c:1752) shifts by `32 - lsb - size` without guarding against a negative count. These are reading findings, not measurements.
