codex
The manuals explicitly make the malformed field cases UNPREDICTABLE and permit arbitrary exceptions; they do not mandate RI. That supports RI as a documented emulator policy.

For the detector, sanitizer silence alone is insufficient: neutralizing the RI helper would avoid the shifts while failing to deliver an exception. The proposed rows therefore need both sanitizer evidence and CPU exception-state checks.
